hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1659","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, narrated to us Zuhayr; and narrated to us Abu Kurayb, narrated to us Sinan — meaning ibn Mutahhir — from Zuhayr, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir (RA), who said:

""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during a journey when it rained. He (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever wishes may pray in his place of residence.'""

**CHAPTER:**"
